 "text": "9/29/26, 9:42 AM\nReg. Fact.      | ---nmnnnnnnn nnn | -----n-nn naan nnn nnn nnn nnn enn |\nMR Res.         0                  800                                    ? kWh\n|\u2014_\u2014\u2014_\u2014\u2014\u2014_- EEE\n|\n\nMR Reas.\n\n08                     09                                      01\n4,000                                           5,000      kWh/Year\nPer.Cons.... |.-@-\u2014\u2014 | _--\n\nWght. Unit                 400               400              200\n\nWght. Por.                 40%               40%            20%\n\nOn installation of the device, a period consumption value of 4,000 kWh/year is entered for the register. This value is changed to\n5,000 kWh / year after the last meter reading result entry in period 09 to O1.\n\nThe minimum portion of weighting in percent is 30%.\nThe sum of the weighting units for one year is 1,000.\n\nWith a weighting portion of 40%, period O09 to 08 is representative. One period consumption change was made in the forecast\nperiod Y to P. The expected meter reading is determined as follows:\n\nFor the period from Y until the period consumption change, extrapolation is based on meter reading results:\n\n1. Determination of meter reading difference 09 to 08: 800 kWh - 0 kWh = 800 kWh\n\na. Determination of consumption for 09 by multiplying the meter reading difference with the register factor: 8300\nkWh2 = 1,600 kWh\n\nb. Determination of consumption per weighting unit: 1,600 kWh: 400 = 4 kWh\n\nc. Extrapolation of consumption for period O09 until the period consumption change: 4 kWh600 = 1,600 kWh\n\nd. Determination of the meter reading difference for period 09 until the period consumption change by dividing the\nconsumption value by the register factor: 1,600 kWh: 10 = 160 kWh\n\n1. For the period from the period consumption change to O1, consumption is extrapolated from the period consumption:\n\na. Determination of period consumption per weighting unit by dividing the period consumption by the weight of\nvalidity period: 5,000 kWh : 1,000 = 5 kWh\n\nb. Extrapolation of period consumption for the period from the period consumption change to 01: 5 kWh200 =\n1,000 kWh\n\nc. Determination of the meter reading difference for the period from the period consumption change to O01 by\ndividing the consumption value by the register factor: 1.000 kWh : 10 = 100 kWh\n\n2. Determination of the expected meter reading for O1 by adding the meter reading difference for meter reading 09: 800\nLANA &1EGN WANA & INN LWh\u2014- TANEGOLWH\n",
